# playpick: mode=raid boss=cold spec=shaman:restoration style=good size=25
# difficulty=heroic view=844x390,touch save=fresh
#
# The Long Cold has never been played by this job. It is the hardest single
# cell in the game (25-heroic, README's own words) and it is a healer's fight
# rather than a tank's or a dps's -- the first two idle/good comparisons in
# direction.md's #1 ("doing nothing wins") were a frost mage and a protection
# warrior, both roles a raid can carry without. A restoration shaman who
# presses nothing heals nobody, which is the sharpest test #1 has had yet:
# if idle still doesn't lose here, the hypothesis gets much harder to explain
# away as "the AI only needed a tank/dps". Fresh save, so 25-heroic is not
# unlocked by the chain -- the invite hash gets there directly, same as the
# doc's own example.
open #b=cold&s=25&h=1
targets
ui
tap class:shaman:restoration
tap pull
waitscreen fight 15
state
shot good-open

play good 200
bill
says
state
shot good-end

# Second pull, same seed (fresh profile has no state to carry, so a fresh
# `open` starts the encounter's pull count back at one) -- this time idle,
# for the direction.md #1 comparison per docs/playtest.md's ladder section:
# discriminate a curve by running idle and good on the same cell and reading
# bill per minute, not just win/lose.
open #b=cold&s=25&h=1
targets
tap class:shaman:restoration
tap pull
waitscreen fight 15
state
shot idle-open

play idle 200
bill
says
state
shot idle-end
